          "memoryCitation": null,
          "phase": "final_answer",
          "questions": null,
          "text": "{\"issues\":[],\"reason\":\"The argument is correct. It identifies the unique pointwise limit, notes that any uniform limit must equal it, and negates uniform convergence with ε=1/2: for every positive integer N, choosing n=N and x=2^{-1/N}∈[0,1) gives |f_n(x)-f(x)|=1/2.\"}",
